<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theophilus Eaton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1590">1590</a>–<a href="/years/1658">1658</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theophilus Eaton (1590–1658) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> merchant who in 1638 founded the New Haven Colony in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> with the Puritan minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-davenport">John Davenport</a>. He served as its governor from 1639 until his death, ruling a strict Puritan settlement in which only church members could vote and biblical law guided the courts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theophilus-eaton.jpg" alt="Theophilus Eaton" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moet9898 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theophilus_Eaton_Governor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
